    "explanation": "Ancient Greek refers to the forms of the Greek language used across the ancient Greek world through several stages—Mycenaean, the Dark Ages, the Archaic or Homeric period, and the Classical period. It was the tongue of epic poets and of fifth‑century Athenian historians, playwrights, and philosophers, and it existed in several regional dialects such as Attic, Ionic, Doric, Aeolic, and Arcadocypriot.\n\nThose dialects mattered because one, Attic, later became the basis for Koine Greek, the common dialect that spread in the Hellenistic era. Ancient Greek has left many words in English and has been studied widely in Western education since the Renaissance.",
